  "notes": "L4v (seL4 verification) repository using Isabelle/HOL. Commit convention: 'tag: action' where tag is the proof session (refine, crefine, ainvs, aspec, lib, clib, word_lib, etc.) optionally prefixed by architecture (arm, aarch64, riscv64, x64). Tags combined with '+' for multi-area commits (e.g. 'refine+crefine:', 'aarch64 crefine:'). Key commit patterns: 'sorry-free'/'close last sorry'/'clear.*sorry' = proof_complete; 'arch-split'/'arch prefix'/'given arch prefix' = refactor (restructuring for multi-architecture support); tag prefix containing aspec/haskell/design/spec = spec_change. 'sorry' used as a standalone proof tactic for WIP/in-progress proofs (historically widespread; now mostly removed); 'oops' for abandoned proofs and tutorial stubs. Main proof sessions: ASpec/aspec (abstract spec), AInvs/ainvs (abstract invariants), Refine/refine (Haskell->Abstract refinement), CRefine/crefine (C->Abstract refinement). Central WP automation: wp, wpsimp, wpc, crunch. C refinement tactics: ctac, csymbr, ceqv, vcg. Corres framework: corres, ccorres, corres_split, ccorres_split. Isar structured proofs use: proof/qed, have/show/hence/thus, obtain, next. Apply-script proofs use: apply.../done. [NO_PROOF] tag in commit body marks commits not requiring proof CI runs. 'quick_and_dirty' mode uses sorry to skip proofs during development.",
